-- #1617/#1618 BYSTANDER — the new machinery is PRESENT and nothing asserted
-- here uses it.
--
-- "The feature works" is what the sibling fixtures test. This one tests the
-- question no gate normally asks: is the code that has NOTHING to do with the
-- change still correct? The change adds a new head-tag bucket (`__fun__`) and
-- makes `headTyNode` peel effect rows, both of which are consulted by EVERY
-- dispatch in the program, not only by the ones that need them.
--
-- 🚨 AN EARLIER VERSION OF THIS FIXTURE COULD NOT FAIL, and an adversarial
-- reviewer falsified it by adding ONE method to its own interface. It declared
-- an arrow impl and an effect impl and then asserted only ORDINARY dispatch,
-- where the goal head is concrete — so the readers the change actually
-- perturbed were never consulted at all. Those readers do not decide ROUTING,
-- they decide ACCEPTANCE, and reaching them needs two shapes the old fixture
-- did not have:
--
--   * an UNDETERMINED constraint (`szc []` fixes nothing). `check` resolves it
--     by COUNTING an interface's impl heads — `implCountForIfaceU >= 2` is
--     `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE`, exit 1. If the arrow and effect impls below were
--     counted, this program would stop COMPILING even though neither is ever
--     dispatched to.
--   * a MULTI-PARAM interface (`Conv`) with an effect-headed sibling impl,
--     which `groundOneObligation` grounds by asking for the UNIQUE impl at a
--     head tag; a second match makes it give up, `b` stays undetermined, and
--     the failure surfaces as a `Display` cascade at `println`.
--
-- Both would go from exit 0 to exit 1 under an acceptance narrowing, which is
-- what makes this fixture able to fail. MEASURED: on the branch commit that had
-- the narrowing (`a8a226cb`) this file is rejected at `check`; on the pre-change
-- base (`aaa43716`) and on the fixed branch it prints the same value below.
--
-- ⚠️ `undeterminedSz` IS NEVER CALLED, AND THAT IS THE POINT, not laziness.
-- `check` still poses the constraint (that is the assertion), while the emitter
-- drops the dead binding — which keeps this fixture BUILDABLE. An undetermined
-- constraint reached from `main` does not build on ANY arm, base included (a
-- single-impl `Sz` with no arrow and no effect anywhere still E-PANICs
-- `no impl of method 'szc' for type 'List'` at `build` on base `aaa43716`);
-- that is a separate, pre-existing defect and this fixture must not import it.
--
-- Expected `(48, True, True)`, hand-derived slot by slot, and byte-identical to
-- what the pre-change compiler printed:
--   1. `unwrap (Box 41)` = 41; `sz True` = 7 via `impl Sz Bool` (NOT the arrow
--      impl, which `Bool` cannot match, and NOT the effect impl, whose head
--      peels to `Float`); 41 + 7 = 48.
--   2. `[1, 2, 3] == [1, 2, 3]` = `True` — prelude dispatch that predates all
--      of this.
--   3. `conv 1` grounds `b` from the UNIQUE `Conv` impl at head `Int` — the
--      effect-headed `Conv (<Stdout> Int) String` is not counted — giving
--      `impl Conv Int Bool`, so `conv 1` is `1 > 0` = `True`.
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int
  szc : List a -> Int

impl Sz Bool where
  sz _ = 7
  szc _ = 21

-- present, never dispatched to
impl Sz (Int -> Int) where
  sz _ = 5
  szc _ = 55

-- present, never dispatched to
impl Sz (<Stdout> Float) where
  sz _ = 6
  szc _ = 66

interface Conv a b where
  conv : a -> b

impl Conv Int Bool where
  conv n = n > 0

-- present, never dispatched to
impl Conv (<Stdout> Int) String where
  conv _ = "never"

data Box a = Box a

unwrap : Box Int -> Int
unwrap (Box n) = n

-- never called: it exists to pose an UNDETERMINED `Sz` constraint at check time
undeterminedSz : Int
undeterminedSz = szc []

main = println (unwrap (Box 41) + sz True, [1, 2, 3] == [1, 2, 3], conv 1)
